{"schema":"SDW_SCRIPTURE_CHAPTER_V1","revision":"52add6f41edc5dd9c21f65f02f933fbd1cec266285bee8bce249607475050398","canonicalSourceHash":"f9dfbce6dd2edfe4bb3b4690acd6622f392035be2b0349df98f3607f0a05f6c2","bookId":"engwebu:job","chapter":23,"verses":[{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":23,"verse_ordinal":551,"verse_start":1,"verse_end":1,"verse_label":"1","text":"Then Job answered,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1740},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":23,"verse_ordinal":552,"verse_start":2,"verse_end":2,"verse_label":"2","text":"“Even today my complaint is rebellious. His hand is heavy in spite of my groaning.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1742},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":23,"verse_ordinal":553,"verse_start":3,"verse_end":3,"verse_label":"3","text":"Oh that I knew where I might find him! That I might come even to his seat!","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1745},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":23,"verse_ordinal":554,"verse_start":4,"verse_end":4,"verse_label":"4","text":"I would set my cause in order before him, and fill my mouth with arguments.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1748},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":23,"verse_ordinal":555,"verse_start":5,"verse_end":5,"verse_label":"5","text":"I would know the words which he would answer me, and understand what he would tell me.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1751},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":23,"verse_ordinal":556,"verse_start":6,"verse_end":6,"verse_label":"6","text":"Would he contend with me in the greatness of his power? No, but he would listen to me.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1754},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":23,"verse_ordinal":557,"verse_start":7,"verse_end":7,"verse_label":"7","text":"There the upright might reason with him, so I should be delivered forever from my judge.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1757},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":23,"verse_ordinal":558,"verse_start":8,"verse_end":8,"verse_label":"8","text":"“If I go east, he is not there. If I go west, I can’t find him.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1761},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":23,"verse_ordinal":559,"verse_start":9,"verse_end":9,"verse_label":"9","text":"He works to the north, but I can’t see him. He turns south, but I can’t catch a glimpse of him.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1764},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":23,"verse_ordinal":560,"verse_start":10,"verse_end":10,"verse_label":"10","text":"But he knows the way that I take. When he has tried me, I will come out like gold.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1768},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":23,"verse_ordinal":561,"verse_start":11,"verse_end":11,"verse_label":"11","text":"My foot has held fast to his steps. I have kept his way, and not turned away.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1771},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":23,"verse_ordinal":562,"verse_start":12,"verse_end":12,"verse_label":"12","text":"I haven’t gone back from the commandment of his lips. I have treasured up the words of his mouth more than my necessary food.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1774},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":23,"verse_ordinal":563,"verse_start":13,"verse_end":13,"verse_label":"13","text":"But he stands alone, and who can oppose him? What his soul desires, even that he does.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1777},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":23,"verse_ordinal":564,"verse_start":14,"verse_end":14,"verse_label":"14","text":"For he performs that which is appointed for me. Many such things are with him.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1780},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":23,"verse_ordinal":565,"verse_start":15,"verse_end":15,"verse_label":"15","text":"Therefore I am terrified at his presence. When I consider, I am afraid of him.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1783},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":23,"verse_ordinal":566,"verse_start":16,"verse_end":16,"verse_label":"16","text":"For God has made my heart faint. The Almighty has terrified me.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1786},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":23,"verse_ordinal":567,"verse_start":17,"verse_end":17,"verse_label":"17","text":"Because I was not cut off before the darkness, neither did he cover the thick darkness from my face.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1789}]}